# Drive media authority

Google Drive is the DAM. Media Assets are Drive files. **Do not persist photos, video, music, voiceovers, or thumbnails on R2.**

## Intake

- Browser → Studio Worker → Google Drive (pipeline-runner Drive client). Then write the Media Asset (`Google Drive File ID` + `Google Drive URL`).
- Do not `STUDIO_MEDIA.put` originals, library tracks, or “temporary” copies that stay after the request.
- Do not store catalog URLs as `https://media.chicagoshining.com/studio/...` on Media Assets.

## Allowed R2 exception

R2 may host a **short-lived public HTTP copy** only when a platform API cannot fetch Drive (`uc?id=` / `webContentLink` is not a Graph/YouTube `cover_url`). That copy is derived from Drive. Drive remains authority. See native grid covers.

## Wrong

```js
await env.STUDIO_MEDIA.put(`studio/music-library/${id}.mp3`, body);
fields["Google Drive URL"] = `https://media.chicagoshining.com/studio/music-library/${id}.mp3`;
```
